# Build and run

Use `build.cmake` with `build_overrides.cmake`. Do not use `ninja_build.bat` or a new CMake preset.

- Qt: `C:/Development/Qt/6.11.2/msvc2022_64`
- Generator: Visual Studio 17 2022, config RelWithDebInfo
- Build dir: `builds/b` (`BUILD_FOLDER` is `b` on purpose; a longer path breaks MSVC moc files past 260 characters)
- App: `builds/b/install/bin/MuseScoreStudio5.exe`

From the repo root:

```powershell
cmake -P build.cmake build install
```

`build` compiles. `install` copies the app into `builds/b/install`. QML and resource edits show up only after install.

Start the app from its install folder, without waiting for it to exit. Starting it from the repo root makes it quit immediately.

```powershell
Start-Process .\builds\b\install\bin\MuseScoreStudio5.exe -WorkingDirectory .\builds\b\install\bin
```

`cmake -P build.cmake run` also launches it, and it holds the shell until MuseScore quits. Arguments after `run` are passed through.

With no arguments, `cmake -P build.cmake` configures only when `builds/b/CMakeCache.txt` is missing, then builds and installs. Delete that tree only for a clean configure: `cmake -P build.cmake clean`.
